window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-46f0e5d2ebd105f5"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"get-your-email-to-inbox-zero\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">将收件箱清理至零未处理邮件</h1> <p>清理积压邮件，用你的语气起草回复，并及时处理新邮件。</p> <p>清理超负荷的收件箱，并查看哪些邮件需要回复、决策或关注。ChatGPT Work 可以提出整理方案、用你的语气起草回复，并按计划检查新邮件。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>清理积压邮件，同时保留有用的邮件记录。</li> <li>按计划找出重要邮件并准备回复草稿。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail（需联网）</a></td> <td>搜索和分类 Gmail 讨论串、创建回复草稿，并在你明确要求时归档、添加标签或移至 Trash。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/outlook-email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">outlook-email（需联网）</a></td> <td>搜索和分类 Outlook 邮件、整理周期性邮件、在你明确要求时更改已读状态或移动邮件，并使用已连接的邮箱起草回复。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>将收件箱清理至零未处理邮件</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请查看我最近 90 天的已连接邮箱，包括已发送邮件。如果我有多个账户，请分别查看。如果我尚未连接任何账户，请说明如何在 ChatGPT Work 的 Plugins（插件）选项卡中连接 Gmail 或 Outlook Email。\n\n推断该收件箱属于工作用途还是个人用途，并识别重要联系人、项目和周期性邮件。使用近期由真人撰写的已发送邮件了解我的写作风格。忽略无法代表我语气的转发邮件或自动生成邮件；如果其他已连接工具可能为回复提供有用背景，也请查看。\n\n请使用自然的标题，为我提供简短、个性化的更新：\n\n- 用一两句话说明你从收件箱中了解到的情况，包括邮件总数和未读数量。\n- 最多列出五封需要关注的邮件。每封用一条简短、以行动为导向的项目符号概括，并提供相关时间和链接。避免猜测，尤其是涉及安全提醒时。\n- 用两到三句话说明哪些日常邮件会被添加标签并归档、哪些邮件会继续显示，以及哪些订阅值得检查。将拟用的 `labels` 以行内代码格式列出，并说明归档的邮件仍可搜索。\n- 用我的语气起草一封有用的回复，简要说明收件人、对方需要什么，以及你发现的相关背景。\n- 说明你之后会做什么，并告诉我可以在此回复来调整你的处理方式。\n- 最后用简单的编号列出三个是/否问题：是否应用清理方案、是否将回复保存为草稿、是否保留建议的检查时间和优先级。给出一行回复示例，例如“1 是，2 是，3 否”，并邀请我补充修改意见。\n\n工作邮件请安排在工作日早上 8 点和下午 4 点检查；个人邮件请安排每天早上 8 点检查。请用第一人称说明：“接下来，我会检查……”说明你会如何提醒我关注新出现或有变化的重要邮件；在相关时使用消息、文档或日历等其他已连接来源；并用我的语气起草回复。告诉我可以在此回复来调整你的处理方式。每次更新都要简洁，在底部列出任何问题；如果没有需要关注的事项，也请简要说明。\n\n未经批准，不要发送、归档或移动任何内容。只执行已批准的整理操作；涉及 Trash 时，始终另行征求批准。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">开始之前</h2> <p>你可以在浏览器或桌面应用中的 ChatGPT Work 里使用此流程。开始前请完成以下事项：</p> <ul> <li><strong>连接邮箱。</strong> 安装 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gmail 或 Outlook Email 插件（需联网）</a>。你也可以连接 Slack、Google Drive 和日历，为起草回复提供更多背景。</li> <li><strong>选择定时检查在哪里运行。</strong> 如果希望在笔记本电脑关闭时仍能继续检查，请从浏览器开始。在桌面应用中，请保持电脑开机并让 ChatGPT 桌面应用持续运行。语音聊天不支持<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/automations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">定时任务（需联网）</a>，因此请在聊天中设置或管理定时任务。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"what-to-expect\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">你可以期待什么</h2> <p>ChatGPT 会查看近期邮件，找出需要关注的内容，提出整理方案，并准备回复草稿，但不会发送邮件。你批准整理方案后，它可以将方案应用到较早的积压邮件。以下是一次对话可能呈现的样子：</p> <p>我查看了你已连接的工作邮箱，重点关注产品发布、文档和生产工作。邮箱中有 <strong>116 封邮件，其中 96 封未读</strong>；大部分未读邮件涉及项目动态、日历更新、共享文件通知和新闻简报。</p> <p><a id=\"what-needs-attention\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">需要关注的事项</h3> <ul> <li><strong>录制准备：</strong> 在明天的录制前，发送对方要求的演示主题、简短个人简介和照片。</li> <li><strong>文档审阅：</strong> 在指南继续推进前，处理有关产品准确性的反馈。</li> <li><strong>预览部署失败：</strong> 在依赖当前变更前，先调查失败的构建。</li> <li><strong>福利事项：</strong> 完成尚未处理的福利变更。</li> <li><strong>登录提醒：</strong> 确认最近的登录是否由你本人发起；如果不是，请按照提醒中的说明处理。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"cleanup\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">收件箱整理</h3> <p>我会将常规项目、日历和文档通知分别添加 <code>Project activity</code>、<code>Calendar</code> 和 <code>Docs</code> 标签后归档；归档邮件仍可搜索。直接请求、正在进行的审阅、失败的构建、安全提醒和所有尚未解决的事项会继续显示。新闻简报和其他周期性订阅值得单独检查。</p> <p><a id=\"a-reply-to-the-recording-organizer\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">回复录制活动组织者</h3> <p>录制活动的组织者正在等你提供演示主题、简短个人简介和照片。我查看了最近的日程背景，并用你的语气起草了回复：</p> <blockquote> <p>很期待这次录制。我准备展示我们讨论过的三个工作流程，今天会把个人简介和照片发给你。我看到了更新后的日历邀请，会按新时间安排。</p> </blockquote> <p>接下来，我会在<strong>每个工作日早上 8 点和下午 4 点</strong>检查。我会提醒你关注新出现或有变化的重要邮件；在相关时查看消息、文档或日历等已连接来源；并用你的语气准备回复。你可以随时回复我来调整处理方式。</p> <p><a id=\"what-would-you-like-me-to-do\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">你希望我怎么做？</h3> <ol> <li><strong>应用这套整理方案吗？</strong> 是 / 否。常规邮件只会被添加标签并归档，不会删除。</li> <li><strong>将这封回复保存为草稿吗？</strong> 是 / 否。</li> <li><strong>保留建议的检查时间和优先级吗？</strong> 是 / 否。</li> </ol> <p>你可以回复“1 是，2 是，3 否”，并补充任何修改意见。</p> <p><strong>警告：</strong> Gmail 插件在你明确要求时可以将邮件移至 Trash。请先查看建议的邮件分组和几个示例；不确定是否需要删除时，请先归档，而不要删除。</p> <p><a id=\"how-it-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">工作原理</h2> <p>邮件工作流程包含几个部分：</p> <ul> <li><strong>已连接的背景信息：</strong> 插件让 ChatGPT 能够读取邮件，并在起草回复需要背景时查看其他已连接工具。Slack 可能包含最新讨论或决策，Google Drive 可能存有相关项目文档，日历则可以帮助确认日期或会议。</li> <li><strong>优先级：</strong> 你可以告诉 ChatGPT 优先处理或忽略哪些联系人、请求、提醒和周期性邮件。后续检查会遵循这些说明。</li> <li><strong>审批边界：</strong> ChatGPT 会提出整理方案并起草回复，但会等待你批准后才采取行动。</li> <li><strong>定时任务：</strong> 你可以让 ChatGPT 按计划检查新邮件，而不必等到你下次回来再提出要求。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"build-your-own-email-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">创建自己的邮件工作流程</h2> <p>如果你已经清楚想要的处理方式，可以提供更具体的要求。<strong>工作邮件</strong>提示词可以重点关注正在进行的对话、请求、截止日期、审批事项和项目背景：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start by reviewing my connected work email account. If you can't access my email, tell me how to connect Gmail or Outlook Email from the Plugins tab in ChatGPT Work.\n\nReview the last 90 days. Keep direct human emails, active conversations, requests, deadlines, approvals, security alerts, HR tasks, and renewals visible. Group recurring project updates, calendar changes, meeting notes, and system notifications so they're easy to find but don't crowd the inbox. Surface newsletters, promotions, and expired reminders for review.\n\nUse recent, human-written sent emails to understand my voice when drafting replies. Check other connected messaging, calendar, or work-context plugins when they might contain relevant information.\n\nGive me a concise, personalized update: briefly describe the inbox and unread count; list up to five emails that need attention, with timing and links; explain in two or three sentences how you'd clean up routine mail while keeping important email visible; and draft one useful reply with enough context to understand who it's for and what they need. End with numbered yes/no questions for cleanup, saving the reply as a draft, and keeping the schedule and priorities, plus a one-line example response.\n\nGoing forward, check my inbox at 8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays. Surface new or changed email that needs my attention, use other connected sources when relevant, and draft useful replies in my voice. Keep each update concise and put any questions at the bottom.\n\nWait for approval before sending, archiving, or moving anything to Trash, and tell me I can change the schedule, priorities, or reply behavior anytime.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">先查看我已连接的工作邮箱账户。如果无法访问邮件，告诉我如何在 ChatGPT Work 的 Plugins（插件）标签页连接 Gmail 或 Outlook Email。\n\n查看过去 90 天的邮件。让人直接发送的邮件、仍在进行的对话、请求、截止日期、批准事项、安全告警、人力资源任务和续订事项保持显眼。将定期项目更新、日历变更、会议记录和系统通知分组，让它们容易找到，同时不挤满收件箱。把新闻简报、促销信息和已过期的提醒列出来供我审阅。\n\n起草回复时，参考近期由我本人撰写并发送的邮件，了解我的表达风格。如果其他已连接的消息、日历或工作上下文插件可能包含相关信息，也要查看。\n\n给我一份简明、个性化的更新：简要描述收件箱状况和未读数量；列出最多五封需要注意的邮件，附上时间信息和链接；用两到三句话解释你会如何整理常规邮件，同时让重要邮件保持显眼；并起草一封有用的回复，提供足够的上下文，让我理解回复对象是谁、对方需要什么。最后用带编号的是/否问题，分别询问是否进行整理、是否将回复保存为草稿，以及是否保留当前检查时间和优先级，并附一行示例答复。\n\n今后，在工作日的上午 8 点和下午 4 点检查我的收件箱。列出新增或发生变化、需要我注意的邮件，相关时使用其他已连接来源，并用我的表达风格起草有用的回复。每次更新保持简短，所有问题放在最后。\n\n发送、归档或移到废纸篓之前，等待我的批准，并告诉我，我可以随时更改检查时间、优先级或回复方式。</div></div> <p><strong>个人邮件</strong>提示词则可以重点关注联系人、账单、包裹、旅行、预约和账户提醒：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start by reviewing my connected personal email account. If you can't access my email, tell me how to connect Gmail or Outlook Email from the Plugins tab in ChatGPT Work.\n\nReview the last 90 days. Keep messages from people I know, bills, renewals, receipts, packages and delivery updates, travel and reservations, appointments, security alerts, and anything time-sensitive visible. Group useful records like order confirmations and account activity so they're easy to find. Surface newsletters, promotions, expired reminders, and recurring subscriptions for review.\n\nUse recent, human-written sent emails to understand my voice when drafting replies. Check my connected calendar or other available context when it might help with a response.\n\nGive me a concise, personalized update: briefly describe the inbox and unread count; list up to five emails that need attention, with timing and links; explain in two or three sentences how you'd clean up routine mail while keeping important email visible; and draft one useful reply with enough context to understand who it's for and what they need. End with numbered yes/no questions for cleanup, saving the reply as a draft, and keeping the schedule and priorities, plus a one-line example response.\n\nGoing forward, check my inbox once each day at 8 AM. Surface new or changed email that needs my attention, use other connected sources when relevant, and draft useful replies in my voice. Keep each update concise and put any questions at the bottom.\n\nWait for approval before sending, archiving, or moving anything to Trash, and tell me I can change the schedule, priorities, or reply behavior anytime.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">先查看我已连接的个人邮箱账户。如果无法访问邮件，告诉我如何在 ChatGPT Work 的 Plugins（插件）标签页连接 Gmail 或 Outlook Email。\n\n查看过去 90 天的邮件。让我认识的人发来的消息、账单、续订、收据、包裹与配送更新、旅行与预订、预约、安全告警，以及任何有时效要求的内容保持显眼。将订单确认、账户活动等有用记录分组，方便查找。把新闻简报、促销信息、已过期的提醒和定期订阅列出来供我审阅。\n\n起草回复时，参考近期由我本人撰写并发送的邮件，了解我的表达风格。如果我已连接的日历或其他可用上下文有助于回复，也要查看。\n\n给我一份简明、个性化的更新：简要描述收件箱状况和未读数量；列出最多五封需要注意的邮件，附上时间信息和链接；用两到三句话解释你会如何整理常规邮件，同时让重要邮件保持显眼；并起草一封有用的回复，提供足够的上下文，让我理解回复对象是谁、对方需要什么。最后用带编号的是/否问题，分别询问是否进行整理、是否将回复保存为草稿，以及是否保留当前检查时间和优先级，并附一行示例答复。\n\n今后，每天上午 8 点检查一次我的收件箱。列出新增或发生变化、需要我注意的邮件，相关时使用其他已连接来源，并用我的表达风格起草有用的回复。每次更新保持简短，所有问题放在最后。\n\n发送、归档或移到废纸篓之前，等待我的批准，并告诉我，我可以随时更改检查时间、优先级或回复方式。</div></div> <p>这两个示例都遵循相同的基本结构：要检查什么、哪些内容重要、要做什么、何时执行，以及哪些操作需要批准。</p> <p><a id=\"take-it-further\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">进一步调整</h2> <p>基本邮件流程开始运行后，你可以继续细化要求，或请 ChatGPT 处理其他有用的邮件任务。</p> <p><strong>始终检查正确的背景信息</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Whenever an email is from [people or teams] or about [project or topic], check [connected source, channel, folder, or doc] before summarizing it or drafting a reply. Call out anything that changes the response.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">只要邮件来自 [people or teams] 或涉及 [project or topic]，就在总结邮件或起草回复之前查看 [connected source, channel, folder, or doc]。指出任何会影响回复的情况。</div></div> <p><strong>起草周期性更新</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Every Friday at 3 PM, draft an email to [people or team] with an update on [project or topic]. Use [connected sources, channels, docs, or files] to summarize progress, decisions, risks, and next steps. Keep it concise and ask me to review before sending.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">每周五下午 3 点，给 [people or team] 起草一封关于 [project or topic] 的进展邮件。使用 [connected sources, channels, docs, or files] 总结进展、决定、风险和后续步骤。保持简短，并在发送前请我审阅。</div></div> <p><strong>跟进尚未收到回复的邮件</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Flag active email threads where I'm waiting on a response and no one has replied in [number] days. Draft a short follow-up using the latest available context, but don't send it without my approval.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">标出那些我正在等待回复、且已经 [number] 天无人回复的进行中邮件讨论串。根据最新可用上下文起草一封简短的跟进邮件，但未经我批准不要发送。</div></div> <p><strong>调整格式</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Organize future inbox checks into “needs a reply,” “waiting on someone,” and “can ignore.” Put anything time-sensitive first.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">今后检查收件箱时，将邮件分为“需要回复”“等待他人”和“可以忽略”。把有时效要求的内容放在最前面。</div></div> <p><strong>说明哪些邮件最重要</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Always surface messages from [people, teams, or senders] and anything about [projects or topics]. Treat [recurring notifications] as low priority.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">始终列出 [people, teams, or senders] 发来的消息，以及任何关于 [projects or topics] 的内容。将 [recurring notifications] 视为低优先级。</div></div> <p><strong>调整回复草稿的方式</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Keep reply drafts short and direct. Match how I normally write, use the latest context from my connected plugins, and ask me when you’re missing context.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">让回复草稿简短直接。符合我平时的写作方式，使用已连接插件中的最新上下文；缺少上下文时向我询问。</div></div> <p><strong>更改检查时间</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check my inbox at 8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays. Only flag messages that need attention before the next check.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">在工作日的上午 8 点和下午 4 点检查我的收件箱。只标出在下次检查之前需要处理或注意的邮件。</div></div> <p>在你信任这些规则之前，清理和回复操作应始终要求你审批。</p> <p>Gmail 和 Outlook 的操作以及定时任务取决于你的套餐和工作区设置。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"get-your-email-to-inbox-zero\">Get your email to inbox zero</h1> <p>Clear the backlog, draft replies in your voice, and stay on top of new email.</p> <p>Clear an overloaded inbox and see which messages need a reply, a decision, or your attention. ChatGPT Work can suggest a cleanup, draft replies in your voice, and check for new email on a schedule.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Clear an overloaded email inbox without losing useful records.</li> <li>Surface important mail and reply drafts on a schedule.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail (online)</a></td> <td>Search and triage Gmail threads, create reply drafts, and archive, label, or move messages to Trash when you explicitly ask.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/outlook-email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">outlook-email (online)</a></td> <td>Search and triage Outlook email, organize recurring messages, change read state or move messages when you explicitly ask, and draft replies using your connected mailbox.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Get your email to inbox zero</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review my connected email from the last 90 days, including sent mail. If I have multiple accounts, review each separately. If none are connected, explain how to connect Gmail or Outlook Email from the Plugins tab in ChatGPT Work.\n\nInfer whether the inbox is work or personal and identify the people, projects, and recurring messages that matter. Use recent, human-written sent emails to understand how I write. Ignore forwarded or generated messages that aren't representative of my voice, and check other connected tools when they might provide useful context for a reply.\n\nGive me a concise, personalized update with natural headings:\n\n- Open with one or two sentences about what you learned from my inbox, including the total and unread counts.\n- List up to five emails that need attention. Keep each to one short, action-oriented bullet with relevant timing and a link. Avoid speculation, especially for security alerts.\n- In two or three sentences, explain what routine email you'd label and archive, what stays visible, and any subscriptions worth reviewing. Format proposed `labels` inline and clarify that archived email remains searchable.\n- Draft one useful reply in my voice, briefly explaining who it's for, what they need, and any relevant context you found.\n- Explain what you'll do going forward and that I can redirect you by replying here.\n- End with three simple, numbered yes/no questions: apply the cleanup, save the reply as a draft, or keep the proposed schedule and priorities. Show how to respond with a one-line example, such as “1 yes, 2 yes, 3 no,” and invite me to include any changes.\n\nSchedule checks at 8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays for work email, or 8 AM daily for personal email. Explain this in first person: “Going forward, I'll check…” Describe how you'll surface new or changed mail that needs attention, use other connected sources like messaging, documents, or calendar when relevant, and draft replies in my voice. Tell me I can redirect you by replying here. Keep each update concise, number any questions at the bottom, and briefly say so if nothing needs attention.\n\nDon't send, archive, or move anything to Trash without approval. Apply only approved cleanup actions and always ask separately before using Trash.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>You can run this in ChatGPT Work in the browser or desktop app. Before you start:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Connect your email.</strong> Install the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gmail or Outlook Email plugin (online)</a>. You can also connect Slack, Google Drive, and your calendar to give ChatGPT more context when drafting replies.</li> <li><strong>Choose where scheduled checks run.</strong> Start in the browser if you want checks to continue when your laptop is off. On desktop, keep your computer on and the ChatGPT desktop app running. Voice chats don't support <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/automations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scheduled tasks (online)</a>, so set up or manage them in chat instead.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"what-to-expect\">What to expect</h2> <p>ChatGPT reviews recent mail, identifies messages that need attention, proposes a cleanup, and prepares replies without sending them. Once you approve the cleanup, it can apply those changes to the older backlog. Here is what that conversation can look like:</p> <p>I reviewed your connected work inbox, centered on product launches, documentation, and production work. It has <strong>116 messages, 96 unread</strong>; most unread mail is project activity, calendar updates, shared-file notifications, and newsletters.</p> <h3 id=\"what-needs-attention\">What needs attention</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Recording prep:</strong> send the requested demo topics, short bio, and photo before tomorrow's session.</li> <li><strong>Documentation review:</strong> address the product-accuracy feedback before the guide moves forward.</li> <li><strong>Failed preview deployment:</strong> investigate the failed build before relying on the current changes.</li> <li><strong>Benefits task:</strong> complete the outstanding benefits change.</li> <li><strong>Sign-in alert:</strong> confirm whether the recent login was yours and follow the alert instructions if it wasn't.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"cleanup\">Cleanup</h3> <p>I'd label and archive routine project, calendar, and document notifications under <code>Project activity</code>, <code>Calendar</code>, and <code>Docs</code>; archived mail remains searchable. Direct requests, active reviews, failed builds, security alerts, and anything unresolved would stay visible. Newsletters and other recurring subscriptions are worth reviewing separately.</p> <h3 id=\"a-reply-to-the-recording-organizer\">A reply to the recording organizer</h3> <p>The recording organizer is waiting on demo topics, a short bio, and a photo. I checked the latest scheduling context and drafted a response in your voice:</p> <blockquote> <p>Excited for this. I'm planning to show the three workflows we discussed and will send the bio and photo today. I saw the updated calendar invite, so I'll plan around the new time.</p> </blockquote> <p>Going forward, I'll check at <strong>8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays</strong>. I'll surface new or changed email that needs your attention, check connected sources like messaging, documents, or your calendar when relevant, and prepare replies in your voice. You can redirect me anytime by replying here.</p> <h3 id=\"what-would-you-like-me-to-do\">What would you like me to do?</h3> <ol> <li><strong>Apply the cleanup?</strong> Yes / no. Routine messages will be labeled and archived, not deleted.</li> <li><strong>Save the reply as a draft?</strong> Yes / no.</li> <li><strong>Keep the proposed schedule and priorities?</strong> Yes / no.</li> </ol> <p>Reply with “1 yes, 2 yes, 3 no” and include any changes.</p> <p><strong>Warning:</strong> The Gmail plugin can move email to Trash when you explicitly ask. Review the proposed groups and a few sample messages first, and archive anything you're unsure about instead of deleting it. Available actions can vary by email plugin and workspace settings.</p> <h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2> <p>An email workflow has a few parts:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Connected context:</strong> plugins let ChatGPT read your email and check other connected tools when a reply needs more context. Slack may have the latest conversation or decision, Google Drive may have relevant files or project docs, and your calendar can clarify dates or meetings.</li> <li><strong>Priorities:</strong> you can tell ChatGPT which people, requests, alerts, and recurring messages to prioritize or ignore. Future checks can use those instructions.</li> <li><strong>Approval boundaries:</strong> ChatGPT proposes cleanup and drafts replies, but waits for your approval before taking action.</li> <li><strong>Scheduled tasks:</strong> instead of waiting for you to come back and ask again, ChatGPT can check for new messages in the same task on a schedule.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"build-your-own-email-workflow\">Build your own email workflow</h2> <p>You can be more specific when you already know what you want. A <strong>work-email</strong> prompt might emphasize active conversations, requests, approvals, and project context:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start by reviewing my connected work email account. If you can't access my email, tell me how to connect Gmail or Outlook Email from the Plugins tab in ChatGPT Work.\n\nReview the last 90 days. Keep direct human emails, active conversations, requests, deadlines, approvals, security alerts, HR tasks, and renewals visible. Group recurring project updates, calendar changes, meeting notes, and system notifications so they're easy to find but don't crowd the inbox. Surface newsletters, promotions, and expired reminders for review.\n\nUse recent, human-written sent emails to understand my voice when drafting replies. Check other connected messaging, calendar, or work-context plugins when they might contain relevant information.\n\nGive me a concise, personalized update: briefly describe the inbox and unread count; list up to five emails that need attention, with timing and links; explain in two or three sentences how you'd clean up routine mail while keeping important email visible; and draft one useful reply with enough context to understand who it's for and what they need. End with numbered yes/no questions for cleanup, saving the reply as a draft, and keeping the schedule and priorities, plus a one-line example response.\n\nGoing forward, check my inbox at 8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays. Surface new or changed email that needs my attention, use other connected sources when relevant, and draft useful replies in my voice. Keep each update concise and put any questions at the bottom.\n\nWait for approval before sending, archiving, or moving anything to Trash, and tell me I can change the schedule, priorities, or reply behavior anytime.\n</code></pre> <p>A <strong>personal-email</strong> prompt might instead emphasize people you know, bills, packages, travel, appointments, and account alerts:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start by reviewing my connected personal email account. If you can't access my email, tell me how to connect Gmail or Outlook Email from the Plugins tab in ChatGPT Work.\n\nReview the last 90 days. Keep messages from people I know, bills, renewals, receipts, packages and delivery updates, travel and reservations, appointments, security alerts, and anything time-sensitive visible. Group useful records like order confirmations and account activity so they're easy to find. Surface newsletters, promotions, expired reminders, and recurring subscriptions for review.\n\nUse recent, human-written sent emails to understand my voice when drafting replies. Check my connected calendar or other available context when it might help with a response.\n\nGive me a concise, personalized update: briefly describe the inbox and unread count; list up to five emails that need attention, with timing and links; explain in two or three sentences how you'd clean up routine mail while keeping important email visible; and draft one useful reply with enough context to understand who it's for and what they need. End with numbered yes/no questions for cleanup, saving the reply as a draft, and keeping the schedule and priorities, plus a one-line example response.\n\nGoing forward, check my inbox once each day at 8 AM. Surface new or changed email that needs my attention, use other connected sources when relevant, and draft useful replies in my voice. Keep each update concise and put any questions at the bottom.\n\nWait for approval before sending, archiving, or moving anything to Trash, and tell me I can change the schedule, priorities, or reply behavior anytime.\n</code></pre> <p>Both examples follow the same basic structure: what to check, what matters, what to do, when to do it, and what requires approval.</p> <h2 id=\"take-it-further\">Take it further</h2> <p>Once the basic workflow is running, you can refine it or ask ChatGPT to handle other useful email tasks.</p> <p><strong>Always check the right context</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Whenever an email is from [people or teams] or about [project or topic], check [connected source, channel, folder, or doc] before summarizing it or drafting a reply. Call out anything that changes the response.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Draft a recurring update</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Every Friday at 3 PM, draft an email to [people or team] with an update on [project or topic]. Use [connected sources, channels, docs, or files] to summarize progress, decisions, risks, and next steps. Keep it concise and ask me to review before sending.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Follow up on unanswered email</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Flag active email threads where I'm waiting on a response and no one has replied in [number] days. Draft a short follow-up using the latest available context, but don't send it without my approval.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Change the format</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Organize future inbox checks into “needs a reply,” “waiting on someone,” and “can ignore.” Put anything time-sensitive first.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Teach it what matters</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Always surface messages from [people, teams, or senders] and anything about [projects or topics]. Treat [recurring notifications] as low priority.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Adjust how it drafts replies</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Keep reply drafts short and direct. Match how I normally write, use the latest context from my connected plugins, and ask me when you’re missing context.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Change when it checks</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check my inbox at 8 AM and 4 PM on weekdays. Only flag messages that need attention before the next check.\n</code></pre> <p>Keep cleanup and reply actions approval-based until you trust the rules.</p> <p>Gmail and Outlook actions and scheduled tasks depend on your plan and workspace settings.</p>"};
